---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { SITE_CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../lib/site";

const crumbs = [{ name: "Home", path: "/" }, { name: "Contact" }];
---

<Layout
  title="Contact"
  description="Contact HomeDIYCalc by email at homediycalc@gmail.com. There is no contact form — the site has no backend — so email is the only contact route."
  canonical="/contact/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">Contact</h1>
  <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-slate-700">
    <p>
      The official contact email for HomeDIYCalc is{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE_CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="font-semibold text-slate-900 underline">{SITE_CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no contact form on this site, and there is no other contact
      address. That is deliberate, not an oversight: the site has no backend
      by design — no server, no database, no form endpoint — so a form that
      appeared to submit a message would be fake. Email is the only way to
      reach us.
    </p>
    <p>
      HomeDIYCalc is operated independently by an individual based in
      Malaysia, not by a company. Emails are read by the operator personally;
      please allow time for a reply. If you are reporting a calculator
      problem, it helps to say which calculator you were using, what you
      entered, and what result you expected — and remember that every
      calculator page publishes its formula, so the math can be checked
      directly.
    </p>
    <p>
      Do not send sensitive personal information by email. Anything you send
      is used only to answer your message; see the{" "}
      <a href="/privacy-policy/" class="underline">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
